# Auth / users / onboarding (P0 — security)

> `.cursor/rules/do-not-touch.mdc` (alwaysApply) is the floor. This rule sits above it and adds nothing that loosens it.

Layered auth: `src/proxy.ts` checks only cookie **presence** at the edge (no Prisma/Node) →
authoritative role/session check is server-side (`getSession` / `requireAdmin`, `/admin` layout).
KYC is bound server-side via a claimed `KycInquiry`; the Persona payload `reference-id` is
client-supplied and untrusted.

## Read first
- `docs/AUTH_USERS_CONTEXT.md`
- `docs/DO_NOT_TOUCH.md`

## Must avoid
- Reintroducing `middleware.ts` — Next 16 silently ignores it; the gate MUST be `src/proxy.ts`.
- Trusting the Persona webhook `reference-id` (P0-4) — it is a hint only; bind via the claimed `KycInquiry`.
- Weakening the dev-bypass double gate (`NODE_ENV !== "production"` AND `DEV_AUTH_BYPASS === "1"`).

## Validate before done
- `PROTECTED_PREFIXES` (proxy logic) and `config.matcher` stay in sync — every prefix mirrored, both forms (`/x` + `/x/:path*`).
- `pnpm test` green for auth-lifecycle, totp, persona webhook (`src/lib/auth/__tests__`, `src/lib/onboarding/__tests__`).
- Webhook keeps HMAC SHA-256 + `timingSafeEqual` (length-checked first) AND the claimed-inquiry check (`prisma.kycInquiry.findUnique`); unclaimed → 200 `unclaimed_inquiry`, never approve.

## STOP and ask before
- ANY edit to `src/proxy.ts` (edge gate / matcher).
- Converting `markKycComplete` to a `"use server"` action (D1 — it is internal server-only, not an action).
- Changing argon2id params (`src/lib/auth/password.ts` — OWASP-tuned).
- Removing the anti-enumeration dummy-hash paths in `src/lib/auth/actions.ts` (equalize verify timing on unknown email).
